-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+----------------------+\n| macro declarations     | `[[:source medium batch j] path]`: the definition at `path` of the batch's `j`-th tree is a macro definition; inside   | the frontend,        |\n|                        | the batch envelope this is written `[j path :yin.macro/definition]` (§8.5)                                             | consumed by the      |\n|                        |                                                                                                                        | expander             |\n+------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+----------------------+\n| harvest catalogue      | `[[:source medium batch] h j path]`: occurrence `[j path]` belongs to the `h`-th **original definition** in the        | the frontend or the  |\n|                        | batch's admission order, plain or macro; one original definition shared at several paths has several rows with one     | §9.1 adapter,        |\ntest/yin/repl_test.cljc:157:                                        (:path server)\ntest/yin/repl/serve_test.cljc:81:                                        (:path endpoint)\ntest/yin/repl/serve_test.cljc:105:    (is (= \"/repl\" (:path endpoint)))\ntest/yin/repl/embed_test.cljc:69:        accepted (ws/accept-connection! (:ws-endpoint endpoint) (:path endpoint)\ntest/yin/repl/connect_test.cljc:619:    (is (= \"/repl\" (:path summary)))\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/serving.cljc:252:                            :path (:ws/path descriptor)\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing/coordinate.cljc:11:  (when-not (and (= #{:dao.jing/type :path} (set (keys coordinate)))\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing/coordinate.cljc:37:    :dao.jing/file (file/create-content-file (:path (validate-file!\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing/file.cljc:106:                             {:path path}))\nsrc/